00:39:31.363 --> 00:39:33.152
Well, that's a paradigm.

00:39:33.152 --> 00:39:34.881
Now this is a beautiful concept,

00:39:34.881 --> 00:39:36.262
so let's understand it.

00:39:36.262 --> 00:39:38.815
Cybernetics and paradigms, alright?

00:39:38.815 --> 00:39:40.389
There's a thermostat.

00:39:40.389 --> 00:39:44.899
Now, a thermostat in your home
is a cybernetic instrument.

00:39:44.899 --> 00:39:47.374
Now, I live in Toronto, so
a good part of the year,

00:39:47.374 --> 00:39:49.933
it gets pretty cold there.

00:39:49.933 --> 00:39:53.014
Other parts of the year,
it gets pretty warm.

00:39:53.014 --> 00:39:56.041
But, in the winter, you
would have your thermostat

00:39:56.041 --> 00:40:00.151
set to control the room
temperature at around 70 degrees.

00:40:00.151 --> 00:40:02.376
Now, you could be sitting
there, reading a book

00:40:02.376 --> 00:40:05.064
or something, and all of
a sudden, you feel a draft

00:40:05.064 --> 00:40:08.411
around your feet, and you
start to feel a little cool,

00:40:08.411 --> 00:40:10.118
and you think, what's going on?

00:40:10.118 --> 00:40:13.076
So you go and look at the thermometer,

00:40:13.076 --> 00:40:15.667
and you notice that the
temperature's not 70,

00:40:15.667 --> 00:40:17.917
it's dropped to 65 degrees.

00:40:19.628 --> 00:40:22.310
You start to investigate,
you think, what's wrong?

00:40:22.310 --> 00:40:24.792
And you'll notice, the front door's open.

00:40:24.792 --> 00:40:27.545
Now, it used to be,
when I was a little boy,

00:40:27.545 --> 00:40:28.862
you'd go and check on the furnace,

00:40:28.862 --> 00:40:30.601
'cause maybe the furnace had gone out,

00:40:30.601 --> 00:40:32.255
and you'd have to shake all the ashes down

00:40:32.255 --> 00:40:35.257
