and get it going again.

00:40:35.257 --> 00:40:36.672
Not today.

00:40:36.672 --> 00:40:39.275
Today, we've got cybernetic mechanisms

00:40:39.275 --> 00:40:41.069
hooked up to our heating system.

00:40:41.069 --> 00:40:43.839
You see, the thermostat
measures the deviation

00:40:43.839 --> 00:40:45.060
from the set goal.

00:40:45.060 --> 00:40:47.447
What was the set goal?
The set goal is 70.

00:40:47.447 --> 00:40:51.765
But the temperature is at
65; things have changed.

00:40:51.765 --> 00:40:55.167
The thermostat sends a
message to the furnace,

00:40:55.167 --> 00:40:58.584
and automatically, the fire is turned on.

00:40:59.983 --> 00:41:03.851
The fan's turned on, and the
temperature starts to rise.

00:41:03.851 --> 00:41:06.283
And it gets up to 66, 67,

00:41:06.283 --> 00:41:09.013
68, 69, and it'll take it right back

00:41:09.013 --> 00:41:11.343
until it's back on course, at 70 degrees.

00:41:11.343 --> 00:41:15.260
And then the fire, and
the fan, are turned off.

00:41:16.143 --> 00:41:17.280
Now think of that.

00:41:17.280 --> 00:41:19.986
And it all happens automatically.

00:41:19.986 --> 00:41:22.954
That's a cybernetic mechanism.

00:41:22.954 --> 00:41:24.498
Interesting, isn't it?

